# FS.GG.SDD — regenerable lifecycle output (ADR-0018).
# Per-work-item readiness views are generated by fsgg-sdd and regenerated by
# `fsgg-sdd refresh`. They are transient: ignore by role, never commit, and do
# not re-include per feature. See docs/reference/artifact-taxonomy.md.
# Exception: the compact merge-boundary verdict is durable-generated (ADR-0026).
# `readiness/*/*` (contents, not the directory) is load-bearing — git never
# descends into an excluded directory, so the negation below would be inert.
readiness/*/*
!readiness/*/ship-verdict.json

# rogue3#56 — the top-level readiness ROLL-UPS that no checkout can reproduce.
#
# All three are rewritten by every `./fake.sh build -t Verify` over inputs that are NOT
# reproducible from a checkout, so tracking them made every gate run produce a
# committable diff nobody wanted:
#
#   evidence-graph.md            enumerates whatever is on disk under `readiness/`, and
#                                part of that tree is `readiness/*/*` output above plus
#                                `readiness/logs/*.txt` this very run writes. The list is
#                                a property of the CHECKOUT, not of the repository — at
#                                715bef9 the committed graph recorded 102 sensed files of
#                                which 12 exist in no clean checkout, so every ordinary
#                                run refused to publish (#26) and the committed graph was
#                                frozen: it also OMITTED four tracked files that do exist.
#   performance-evidence.json    measured p50Ms/p95Ms/p99Ms and allocatedBytes, plus the
#                                inputDigest/receiptDigest/artifactDigest over them and a
#                                compositionAuthority MVID that moves whenever the assembly
#                                is rebuilt (src/Rogue3/PerformanceEvidence.fs). 39 leaves
#                                differed between origin/main and one gate run at 715bef9.
#   m7-ui-performance.json       measured p95Ms/p99Ms and NOTHING else -- it carries no
#                                p50Ms, no allocatedBytes and no compositionAuthority at
#                                all. 8 leaves differed over the same run. The two files
#                                are grouped here because both are irreproducible, not
#                                because they record the same things.
#
# DELIBERATELY NOT LISTED: `readiness/performance-critic-request.json`. It digests
# performance-evidence.json and is irreproducible for the same reason, but it is written
# only by `-t PerformanceCriticRequest`, which `Verify` never calls — so it has never
# dirtied a gate run, and untracking it would have deleted a record while buying no part
# of this item's acceptance. It stays tracked, refreshed deliberately by its own target,
# and its digest over an artifact the repository no longer carries is a historical
# statement of the same kind a merged audit makes.
#
# What stays TRACKED, and where a reviewer should actually look:
#   readiness/performance-intent.yml       all 7 workload ids, definition digests and the
#                                          p95/p99/catch-up/structural-cost budgets. It
#                                          carries NO UI-route information.
#   src/Rogue3/EvidenceCommands.fs         the four UI-route definition strings and their
#                                          DECLARED definition digests, which is where the
#                                          m7 route coverage is really pinned.
#   readiness/evidence-audit.md            the verdict and node count. Checkout-stable, and
#                                          the control case for the whole diagnosis: tracked
#                                          roll-ups are fine, roll-ups that enumerate
#                                          irreproducible things are not.
#   layout-evidence.txt / headless-scene-evidence.txt   the baseline the gate requires.
#
# WHAT LEAVES GIT, stated plainly rather than implied: the measured percentiles and
# allocations themselves, and the four UI routes' `observedScale` (retained/bound control
# counts and per-output named-region rectangles) with their authorship/scale verdicts.
# Merged SDD evidence under `work/` and `docs/roguelike-dungeon-crawler-roadmap.md` cite
# these artifacts as committed records and can no longer be read that way; that is the
# cost rogue3#56 names for this option, and it is paid here rather than hidden.
#
# Consequence for the audit-binding gate: a merged audit that cited one of these pinned a
# sha256 over a run output. Those citations cannot be checked from a repository that does
# not carry the bytes, and `scripts/check-audit-bindings.py` reports them under `notBound`
# rather than checking them, keyed on THIS list.
#
# What that keying does and does NOT buy. It makes widening the exemption a two-file
# change a reviewer can see, and removing (or negating) a line here withdraws the
# exemption and fails the checker. It does NOT detect re-tracking: a `.gitignore` rule has
# no effect on a file already in the index, and the checker deliberately never asks git
# what is tracked (a checker that did would exempt everything in an export with no
# repository). The check that the index and this list agree is a CI step —
# `.github/workflows/verify.yml`, "Derived roll-ups stay out of the index".
readiness/evidence-graph.md
readiness/performance-evidence.json
readiness/m7-ui-performance.json

# Generic build & tooling output.
bin/
obj/
artifacts/
TestResults/
.tmp/
nuget-cache/
